// Title: Persistence Via New SIP Provider
// ID: 5a2b21ee-6aaa-4234-ac9d-59a59edf90a1
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-21
// Tags: attack.persistence, attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1553.003
// Description: Detects when an attacker register a new SIP provider for persistence and defense evasion
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "\\Dll") OR where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "\\$DLL"))) AND ((where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Cryptography\\Providers\\") OR where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Cryptography\\OID\\EncodingType") OR where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "\\SOFTWARE\\WOW6432Node\\Microsoft\\Cryptography\\Providers\\") OR where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "\\SOFTWARE\\WOW6432Node\\Microsoft\\Cryptography\\OID\\EncodingType")))) AND NOT ((((where(Details = "WINTRUST.DLL") OR where(Details = "mso.dll"))) OR (where(Image = "C:\\Windows\\System32\\poqexec.exe") AND where(TargetObject ICONTAINS "\\CryptSIPDll") AND where(Details = "C:\\Windows\\System32\\PsfSip.dll")))))
